[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m Using Legendre's formula to find the exponents of primes in $9!$:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m - Prime 2: $\left\lfloor \frac{9}{2} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{9}{4} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{9}{8} \right\rfloor = 4 + 2 + 1 = 7$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m - Prime 3: $\left\lfloor \frac{9}{3} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{9}{9} \right\rfloor = 3 + 1 = 4$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m - Prime 5: $\left\lfloor \frac{9}{5} \right\rfloor = 1$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m - Prime 7: $\left\lfloor \frac{9}{7} \right\rfloor = 1$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m So, the prime factorization of $9!$ is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=157529)[0m 9! = 2^7 \times 3^4 \times 5^1 \times 7^1
